  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 230 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nPotential for brief heat relief early next week:\n\nThe pattern begins to shift a bit after Sunday. Global ensembles\ndepict the mid- and upper-level ridge flattening, sagging the\njet stream and associated surface stationary front closer to our\narea. As a result, temperatures may decrease and precipitation\nchances may increase - at least for a day or two.\n\nDeterministic models hint at a subtle shortwave moving just \nnortheast of the area Sunday night, which would force a cold \nfront through the area. This places 20-40% chances of rain over\nthe area Monday, with high temperatures noticeably cooler\nranging from 87 in central MO, to 98 along the southern MO\nborder. NBM temperatures spreads depict some uncertainty in\nexactly where the front is positioned during peak heating\nMonday, leading to high temperatures anywhere from the middle\n80s to upper 90s for Springfield alone. \n\nModel spread increases even more after Monday with 59% of 12Z\nLREF members suggesting ridging to build back into the area,\nwhile 41% of members show a greater geopotential height gradient\nand northwesterly flow over our area. This leads to spreads in\ntemperatures and precipitation chances. For these days. Trends\nin the forecast will continue to be monitored for if heat\ntries to make a return, or if precipitation chances try to\nincrease before the end of meteorological summer.",
